IntTools_FClass2d: a point on a face whose parameter range spans many
periods is classified at every copy of it in the range (mitcad#349).

IntTools_FClass2d::Perform and TestOnRestriction, asked to try the
periods of a periodic surface (RecadreOnPeriodic), classify the point as
given, then move it into the face's parameter range
(GeomInt::AdjustPeriodic) and try that copy and the copies a period, two
periods and so on above it, up to the range's end. AdjustPeriodic leaves a
point that is already in the range where it is, so the copies below it
were never tried. On a face of one period that makes no difference; on a
threaded hole's cylinder kept as one face between helices running 32
turns, a section curve's point given in the surface's first period
(u about 6) lay in the range, but the copy inside the face was 16 periods
below it: the point was classified as outside, and the booleans dropped the
parts of section curves on that face (a box cut across the thread removed
nothing).

The tried copies now start at the first one at or above the range's start
(as BRepTopAdaptor_FClass2d already does), so that every copy in the range
is tried. Faces whose range spans at most one period try the same copies as
before.

--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/IntTools/IntTools_FClass2d.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/IntTools/IntTools_FClass2d.cxx
@@ -52,6 +52,17 @@
   #include <Geom2d_BSplineCurve.hxx>
 #endif
 
+#include <cmath>
+
+//=================================================================================================
+
+// Mitcad (mitcad#349): the copy of a parameter of a periodic surface by
+// whole periods that is the first one at or above theMin.
+static double FirstCopyInRange(const double theValue, const double theMin, const double thePeriod)
+{
+  return theValue - std::floor((theValue - theMin) / thePeriod) * thePeriod;
+}
+
 //=================================================================================================
 
 IntTools_FClass2d::IntTools_FClass2d() = default;
@@ -669,11 +680,15 @@ TopAbs_State IntTools_FClass2d::Perform(const gp_Pnt2d& _Puv, const bool Recadre
     if (IsUPer)
     {
       GeomInt::AdjustPeriodic(uu, Umin, Umax, uperiod, uu, du);
+      // The copies are tried upwards from here: start at the first one in
+      // the range, also on faces spanning several periods (mitcad#349).
+      uu = FirstCopyInRange(uu, Umin, uperiod);
     } // if (IsUPer) {
     //
     if (IsVPer)
     {
       GeomInt::AdjustPeriodic(vv, Vmin, Vmax, vperiod, vv, dv);
+      vv = FirstCopyInRange(vv, Vmin, vperiod);
     } // if (IsVPer) {
   }
   //
@@ -836,11 +851,15 @@ TopAbs_State IntTools_FClass2d::TestOnRestriction(const gp_Pnt2d& _Puv,
     if (IsUPer)
     {
       GeomInt::AdjustPeriodic(uu, Umin, Umax, uperiod, uu, du);
+      // The copies are tried upwards from here: start at the first one in
+      // the range, also on faces spanning several periods (mitcad#349).
+      uu = FirstCopyInRange(uu, Umin, uperiod);
     } // if (IsUPer) {
     //
     if (IsVPer)
     {
       GeomInt::AdjustPeriodic(vv, Vmin, Vmax, vperiod, vv, dv);
+      vv = FirstCopyInRange(vv, Vmin, vperiod);
     } // if (IsVPer) {
   }
